menu "ENC28J60 (vendored)"

config ENC28J60_POLL_MS
    int "Service the chip every N ms regardless of the INT line (0 = interrupt only)"
    default 20
    range 0 1000
    help
      Upstream relies entirely on the INT pin. If that line is unwired, noisy,
      or misses an edge, transmit-complete is never serviced and the ENC28J60
      transmit engine can stay locked with TXRTS asserted -- the link looks up
      but nothing can be sent.

      With a non-zero value the driver also wakes on this interval and reads
      the interrupt flags over SPI. Interrupts still work and still shorten the
      wait, so this is a floor rather than a replacement. 20 ms costs two
      register reads per poll and makes the INT wire optional.

      Set 0 to restore upstream interrupt-only behaviour.

endmenu
